course: dictionary
lesson: 15392
title: Spelt: one word, several jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Spelt» is the past tense of the verb «spell». Yesterday Priya spelt her name correctly. Here it means she wrote the letters in the right order. In British English we say «spelt»; in America people usually say «spelled».
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «Dad bought spelt flour to bake bread.» The word flour is the clue, so spelt is a kind of wheat here, not a verb. Ask yourself: is this an action, or a thing?
explain: Spelt can also mean caused or meant, in an informal way. «The grey clouds spelt trouble for our picnic» means the clouds showed that trouble was coming. Try putting "meant" or "showed" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: «Spelt» is the past tense of the verb «spell», and it is the usual British form.
fact: In American English, people usually write «spelled» instead.
fact: Spelt is also a kind of old wheat, used to make flour and bread. You say some spelt, not two spelts.
fact: «Spelt out» means explained very clearly. «Spelt trouble» means it showed that trouble was coming.
fact: Check the clue words: if the sentence is about letters or writing, spelt is the verb; if it is about bread or flour, it is the grain.
exercise: «Yesterday Priya spelt her name correctly on every line.» What does spelt mean here? | *Wrote the letters in the right order | Explained very clearly | Caused a disaster | Cleaned the words off the page
exercise: «Dad bought spelt flour to bake bread.» What is spelt in this sentence? | A fast car | *A kind of old wheat grain | A type of school bag | A sort of sweet
exercise: «The dark clouds spelt trouble for our picnic.» What does spelt mean? | Cleaned up | *Meant or caused | Hid or buried | Wrote down
test: Which word is the past tense of «spell» in British English? | spelling | *spelt | spell | spells
test: «The fog spelt danger for the ships.» What does spelt mean here? | Wrote down | Cleaned | Ate | *Meant or caused
exam: In «She spelt out the plan, step by step, so everyone understood», what does spelt out mean? | Spelled it wrong | Wrote the plan on paper | *Explained very clearly | Put out a fire
